# I04.var05 v1.0.2 supplemental receipt reader — GO_METHOD_CONSTRUCTION_ONLY

Decision: **GO_SUPPLEMENTAL_METHOD_CONSTRUCTION**, limited to an exact CRLF-preserving copy of the frozen 88,398-byte independent reader into the predeclared future path `review/independent-postrun-receipt-reader-v1.py`, followed by precisely two additions within `verify_checker_receipts`: add `native_run_directory` to the exact behavior receipt key set; require `type(behavior["native_run_directory"]) is str` and exact equality to `str(RUN)` immediately after the existing behavior schema/pass check. The original reader, prelaunch inventory and manifest, 25 sealed run originals, and recovered copies remain unchanged. This is not postrun acceptance.

The frozen prospective recovery contract `tmp/i04-var05-v102-postrun-receipt-schema-recovery-v1-20261008.json` is 5,329/SHA-256 `65cb30fe750037ce049f982b126c59e1a72dd387753f78003dace4021029d5ce`. I independently rehashed every declared reader, author receipt, failed replay receipt/stream, NO_GO, native seal, manifest, approval, invocation, closure, model log, raw report and converter log pin. The actual author receipt has exactly one key beyond the frozen reader's expected set: `native_run_directory`, a string equal to the approved short physical path. The first reader failure remains formal `NO_GO_POSTRUN_AS_FROZEN` (2,572/SHA-256 `dcfd7bceee7df9c6fa717e05c30949f765e18cf03e8a6407c6ce552e5523c1a4`).

Before any supplemental replay, an independent byte audit must prove reverse application of the two additions recovers the frozen reader exactly and that every other byte is identical. Separate in-memory cloned behavior receipts must reject missing field, wrong path, non-string value and unknown extra key without modifying sealed evidence. Root must capture the method audit's original binary streams and integer exit. Only a separately reviewed exact method and negative proof may be run once against unchanged read-only recovered copies; that result requires its own bounded postrun decision. No SIMLOX, accepted parent checker, author checker or publication mutation is authorized here.
